<h1>About</h1>
<p>I'm <strong>Himanshu Sardana</strong> — a developer who lives in the terminal. <strong>Arch</strong> (i3 / Hyprland), <strong>Neovim</strong>, and a mild obsession with fast, minimal software.</p>
<p>I build <strong>developer tools and systems projects</strong>: a Kafka clone in Go (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/camus" style="color:#f5f5f5">camus</a>), a TUI manga reader (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/manga-tui" style="color:#f5f5f5">manga-tui</a>), a static site generator (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/kite" style="color:#f5f5f5">kite</a>), a minimal git frontend (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/bonsai" style="color:#f5f5f5">bonsai</a>), and competitive-programming tooling (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/cpos" style="color:#f5f5f5">cpos</a>).</p>
<p>Day to day: <strong>Go, Python, TypeScript / Svelte</strong> — plus Tauri, SQLite, ChromaDB and LLM APIs.</p>
